# Survey Command Center

## Scope

- Change only Command Center UI/filter/data paths required by the task.
- Do not redesign unrelated pages or refactor QC / Registry / Demand / Report workflows.
- Do not delete New Survey routes, APIs, or permissions when removing the header button from this page.

## Data & filters

- Treat Smart Filter state as the single source of truth for KPIs and ward cards.
- Respect District → ULB → Ward cascade; clear invalid child selections after parent changes.
- Never send sentinel values (`all`, `any`) as database IDs unless the backend explicitly supports them.
- Reuse existing survey status buckets (`survey-bucket.util`) — do not invent new completed/draft definitions.
- Use existing UTC date/month helpers already used by Command Center; do not hardcode IST without an explicit product decision.
- Ward lists: numeric ward-number ascending (`sortWardsByNumberAsc` / `compareWardNumbersAsc`). Display both number and name.

## Surveyor data on ward cards

- Ward card `activeSurveyors` counts remain allowed where already implemented.
- Do not reintroduce a dedicated Surveyor Activity section on Command Center unless explicitly requested.

## Safety

- No schema/migrations, env, Docker, auth guard, or API contract breaking changes unless explicitly requested.
- Additive API fields/endpoints only; do not remove existing response properties.
- After changes: `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, relevant tests; review git diff and drop unrelated edits.
